WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.330
A hue shift in HSV space becomes, in RGB space,

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:08.740
a rotation around the gray diagonal from black to white.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:13.150
The authors formalize this as the group H-n of n
discrete rotations about that diagonal,

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:17.560
a subgroup of all three-dimensional rotations.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:21.970
A Color Equivariant Convolution correlates the
input with hue-rotated copies of each filter,

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:26.380
producing feature maps that carry an extra
dimension indexing the hue rotation.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.790
In hidden layers,

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:35.200
filters are cyclically permuted across this
dimension so equivariance is preserved throughout the network.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.610
Because the extra dimension multiplies the number
of feature maps,

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:44.020
the authors decompose filters into spatial and
pointwise components and offer hybrid variants

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.430
that use color equivariance only in the early,

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:52.840
most color-selective stages, keeping parameter and
compute cost in check.
